{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# Phase 2 (Repair) — scoped to the `search_files` path defect\n\nGerrit change **1433** — `bf31: search_files must not fake \"(no matches)\"`\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1433\n\n## Files in the diff (2)\n\n* `src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py` (+43 −19)\n* `tests/unit/test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py` (new, 10 cases)\n\n## RED evidence (before any fix existed)\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py -q\n    -> 6 failed, 3 passed        (exit 1)\n\nThe 6 failures are the three file-path-with-hit cases and the three nonexistent-path cases; each\nfails on the specific assertion that `\"(no matches)\"` was returned for a literal that is present, or\nfor a path that cannot be searched. The **3 that passed pre-fix are the ones that must not regress**\n— honest absence, the directory branch, and root confinement — so the oracle is not merely failing\neverywhere.\n\n## Held-out discipline\n\nThe test file was **moved out of the fixer's working tree** (`/tmp/bf31-heldout/`) before the\nimplementation subagent was launched, and the subagent was given only the confirmed mechanism, the\nreproduction, and a prose contract card — never the fixture, assertions, or path. It was told not to\ncreate or look for tests. GREEN was verified by re-applying the held-out oracle afterwards:\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py -q  ->  10 passed  (exit 0)\n\n## Mutation checks (both required, both performed)\n\n1. **Re-introduced the exact root cause** — deleted the file/missing-path discrimination so\n   `os.walk` silently yields nothing again: **6 failed (exit 1)**; restoring the fix: 10 passed\n   (exit 0). The oracle has teeth against the original defect.\n2. **Applied the discovery filter to the file branch** (the subtle re-introduction the plan review's\n   G6 finding predicted): **1 failed (exit 1)**; restored: 10 passed (exit 0).\n\nMutation 2 mattered. My **first** version of that test was vacuous — its `tmp_path` root was not a\ngit repo, so `_git_tracked` returned `None`, `skip_file` never fired, and the assertion could not\nfail. The mutation check exposed it (`MUTATION2_EXIT=0`), and the case was rewritten with a real git\nrepo, a `.gitignore`d file, and an explicit pre-assertion that the filter is genuinely armed before\nthe real assertion is trusted. An assertion that cannot fail is not evidence.\n\n## Gates (real exit codes)\n\n| gate | exit |\n|---|---|\n| `pytest tests/unit/test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py -q` | 0 (10 passed) |\n| `make lint` | 0 |\n| `make typecheck` | 0 (mypy, 435 files) |\n| `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q` | 1 — **1 pre-existing failure**, 10440 passed, 46 skipped |\n\nThe single CI failure is `tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py::test_full_backend_account_is_present`.\nVerified pre-existing: re-run with this change **stashed**, on a clean tree at `origin/main`\n`68ae305cef`, it still fails identically (exit 1). Filed as [rebar:354d-c85d-6689-4302].\n\n## Fix-safety audit\n\n* **Restoration, not creation** — no new entry point, command or user-visible artifact; two cases\n  that returned a false `\"(no matches)\"` now return a true hit list and an explicit error.\n* **No new dependency** — `os` only, already imported.\n* **No test weakened** — no pre-existing test was touched (`git diff --stat` = 2 files, one new).\n* **Directory branch held** — the caller-dependency sweep found every gate reaches this tool through\n  the directory branch, which is byte-identical (shared `scan_one` helper preserves the hit format\n  and both caps) and now pinned by a regression test.\n\n## Step 7 sweep\n\n* **Construct axis** — swept every `os.walk(` in `src/rebar` (8 sites). The other 7 take\n  internally-derived roots (snapshot dirs, `repo_root`, cache paths), never an agent-supplied path.\n  No siblings.\n* **Parity axis** — rule: *a read-only agent tool must not report an unsearchable path as an honest\n  empty result*. Census, each probed live: `list_directory(FILE)` -> `Error: Not a directory` OK;\n  `list_directory(MISSING)` -> `Error` OK; `read_file(DIRECTORY)` -> `Error: Is a directory` OK;\n  `read_file(MISSING)` -> `Error` OK; `search_files` was the **sole MISSING slot** — fixed.\n  One residual gap: `read_file` with an inverted line range silently reads to EOF -> filed as\n  [rebar:4c2b-7b86-913e-40ee].\n\n## Deferred, filed and linked `discovered_from` this ticket\n\n* [rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e] — no loop breaker: `tool_step_limit` never set on the primary verify step\n* [rebar:fd84-92b4-01ba-4911] — bounded recovery unreachable for a step-budget `LLMRunnerError`\n* [rebar:8b97-a0ca-82a4-4d4e] — repetition diagnostic computed then dropped\n* [rebar:218e-0ec1-385d-493a] — `--force-close` offered as the remedy for a RESOURCE exhaustion\n* [rebar:4c2b-7b86-913e-40ee] — `read_file` inverted-range silent read-to-EOF\n* [rebar:354d-c85d-6689-4302] — pre-existing CI red on `main`\n\n## Replication — what this predicts for e369\n\nReplaying **all 187 `search_files` calls the failed run actually made** against the fixed tool:\n\n* **72** that returned `\"(no matches)\"` now return real hits — they were lies;\n* 83 were honest absences and are unchanged; 32 already had hits and are unchanged.\n\nThe loop's decisive call is broken at the source:\n\n    search_files(\"J1\", \"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_characterization.py\")\n    before: \"(no matches)\"   (31 times, driving the cycle)\n    after : \"...:116: # J1 (rebar-ticket acb2-1823-2f0d-415b) — extraction oracles.\"\n\n**Prediction, stated precisely:** this removes the *proven* cause of the non-convergence, so the\nclose should now RUN TO A VERDICT rather than exhaust. It does **not** predict the verdict is PASS.\nTwo residual risks, both outside this fix's scope: there is still no loop breaker\n([rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e]), so a different loop could form; and the epic's criterion #1 (\"every\nchild story is closed and its change is `Verified +1` on Gerrit\") is not checkable from the\nrepository at all — the Gerrit half has no evidence any tool here can reach, and the deterministic\nchild-closure proof the precheck already computed is never surfaced to the verifier. That criterion\nis the most likely route to a genuine FAIL."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785932805848860001,"uuid":"f31cdca0-2873-4d36-829b-56d332eaaeff"}